-- title:
--   X Evaluated Slice BABAtensor Avg Eq X Full Data
-- statement:
--   **The evaluated-slice $BAB$ tensor average equals its mixed full-data average.**
--
--   Let $(q,m,d)$ have a field model, let $S$ be a symmetric strategy on the successor space, and let `family` be a slice-indexed polynomial submeasurement family. The quantity `xEvaluatedSliceBABAtensorAvg` can be reindexed as a uniform average over a point $u$ and a full-slice question $Q=(Q_1,Q_2)$. For $A$ equal to the evaluation at $u$ of the first slice measurement and $B$ equal to the second slice measurement, the value is
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb{E}_{(u,Q)\sim\mathrm{Unif}(\mathrm{Point}\times\mathrm{FullSliceQuestion)}}
--   \left[\sum_{a\in\mathbb{F}_q}\sum_h
--   \operatorname{ev}_S\!\left((B_h A_a B_h)\otimes(A_a)\right)\right].
--   $$
--
--   Here $h$ ranges over global polynomial outcomes, $A_a$ is the outcome-$a$ effect of the evaluated first slice measurement, and $B_h$ is the outcome-$h$ effect of the second slice measurement. Thus this expression is exactly equal to `xEvaluatedSliceBABAtensorAvg`, with no error term. It is the reindexing step used by `xEvaluatedSliceBABAtensor_to_xEvaluatedFullSliceABABAvg`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.xEvaluatedSliceBABAtensorAvg_eq_xFullData`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
